## 7. Required checks

Use a separate scratch data directory and Unity project; never use the main project for fixtures or access scene storage directly. Compile importer changes through `scripts/compile-unity.sh` where available. Use a real Unity harness for serialized references, prefab behavior and Undo, not C# compile alone. Run `npm test` and `npm run typecheck` for implementation increments; browser/server checks are required if those surfaces change.

1. Existing mappings load unchanged, all fields remain editable, and Undo restores them. Search and fallback previews work without a loaded Level. Unknown entries remain visible.
2. Two instances of one entity resolve to different NPCs; a third inherits globally. Source movement/rotation/scale and visibility update correctly, including offsets and kept blockout alignment.
3. Picker cancellation changes nothing; choosing a prefab and Clear override each apply immediately and undo atomically without navigating to the Level or syncing unrelated nodes. A global mapping change affects the inheriting instance without overwriting local replacement settings. Clearing one override restores inheritance. Editing one exception leaves unrelated objects/shared entity assets untouched.
4. User children, supported root components and stable-root references survive sync and supported swaps. Internal prefab references/edits receive the documented conflict behavior; there is no silent loss. Verify migration from existing root-prefab scenes.
5. Claim, drift, Revert, no-collisions, tags, cut blockouts and terrain protections continue to work.
6. Missing prefab, deleted/restored source node, changed source entity/type, duplicate source instance, duplicate Level, same scene in two Levels and different source scene with colliding node IDs behave as specified.
7. Save/reopen, domain reload, Undo/Redo of record edits and Sync, unchanged-export Sync, export-driven Auto sync and failure rollback preserve settings and representation consistently.
8. Orlando can find and edit the screenshot's mappings quickly, then move two distinct NPCs from orlablocks without reassigning them or breaking supported gameplay references. Only Orlando can mark this hands-on acceptance complete.

